omx-contract (0.23.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * test: the md render's param page says since 0.1.0
  * renders: the committed header and json say since 0.1.0, rendered from the
    reset domains
  * domains: a domain's info.version is the vocabulary's own, at 0.1.0, never
    its package's
  * semver: a tag of another major is refused by name, exit 2
  * format: every domain document and manifest states x-omx-contract, and
    every reader holds it
  * docs/contract-dir: every domain document and manifest states its format,
    x-omx-contract
  * schema: omx-contract's format is 0.23.0, its ids v0
  * packaging and docs: omx-contract's own data is <contractdir>/omx-contract/
  * contract directory: the installer and the reader have no schema-major
    level
  * docs/contract-dir: the contract directory has no schema-major level
  * release: the bump is held to the newest tag of package.json's major
  * version: omx-contract is 0.23.0, and its two domains are 0.23.0 with no
    x-since above it
  * render json: the vocabulary schema's $id names the schema's major, never
    the package version's
  * test: the rpm-on-tag sabotage arm finds the rpm job's devel-push condition
  * release: a merge to devel publishes the real package to staging
  * publish.yml: only the dry-run-only promote jobs may be skipped; every
    other promote job must succeed
  * publish.yml: a skipped dry-run-only promote job passes the npm gate; the
    channel jobs must each succeed
  * omx-contract 3.23.0: the changes since 3.22.0 are MINOR
  * install-cli: the CLI tree carries the example descriptors its
    package.json exports
  * domain format: a reply code's x-leaves-no-mark is the data form's
    leavesNoMark
  * param-units-clap-encoded test: the item ships in 3.22.0, the domain may
    be a later 3.x
  * param domain 3.23.0: PARAM_FILTER_RESPONSES is new in 3.23.0
  * docs/render.md, CHANGELOG: --data --with-domain names the domain document
    in its provenance (#241)
  * render --data --with-domain: a rebuilt file names its domain document in
    every provenance line
  * filter-response test: no pin of omx-dsp's copy; omx-dsp reads the item
  * descriptor: a filter control states its response, a word of
    PARAM_FILTER_RESPONSES
  * render ts: a domain's module names its domain document in GENERATED

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:19:26 +0000
